a-p4 : Block
a-p4 = prose (cons "The equivalence class of \((a,b)\) represents \(a-b\). Addition is induced by \((a,b)+(c,d)=(a+c,b+d)\), and its well-definedness is proved from the defining equality. Rationals arise from integer pairs \((p,q)\) with \(q\ne0\), identified when \(ps=rq\) for \((p,q)\) and \((r,s)\). The sign and nonzero-denominator conditions belong to the construction; they are not omitted in the name of abstraction." nil)
